# ============================================================================
# Environment variables template — SAFE TO COMMIT AND SHARE
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values there. The real `.env` is
# gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# Convention for this project: every secret (API key, access token, password,
# database URL, connection string, webhook secret) lives in `.env` as
# NAME=value on its own line, is referenced from code via its variable name,
# and gets a blank/placeholder entry added here under the matching section.
#
# NOTE: the app itself (index.html) is fully offline and client-side — it uses
# no secrets and cannot read environment variables from the browser. These
# files exist for any future server, build step, script, or API integration.
# Never put a secret in index.html: anything in that file ships to every
# machine the file is opened on.
# ============================================================================

# --- No services connected yet. Add variables below as they are introduced ---
# Example format:
# SERVICE_NAME_API_KEY=
# DATABASE_URL=
